WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:02.590
- [Narrator] If you've
ever seen a commercial

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:05.630
for the Home Depot, you might
be familiar with this tune.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.240
- [Man] It's a good time to be a doer.

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.180
- [Narrator] Home Depot and its theme song

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:12.963
have inspired a wave of
videos on social media,

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.020
revealing its cultural status

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.080
as the go-to home improvement store

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:19.543
for many during the pandemic.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.960
Home Depot is the world's
largest home improvement retailer

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.480
with over 2300 stores
across North America.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.280
- What we've seen is
home price appreciation

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:33.870
and housing activity at
unprecedented levels.

00:00:33.870 --> 00:00:37.290
And what we know is that when
homes become more valuable

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:39.760
those homeowners are more
willing to spend on them.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.870
- [Narrator] With its
2021 fiscal year sales

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:44.890
larger than both Lowe's
and ACE Hardware combined,

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.950
one of Home Depot's biggest advantages

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:49.610
is its foothold in the
professional customer space.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.520
That is electricians,
remodelers, plumbers,

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.780
and other home professionals

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.780
that place more lucrative orders.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.500
So how exactly has Home Depot

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.210
attracted more professional customers

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.090
and what other strategies have helped it

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.760
become a leader in the home
improvement retail industry?

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.120
This is the economics of Home Depot.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.360
- Walking into a Home Depot

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.080
you'll see a huge floor space,

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.350
dozens of long aisles with
everything from screws

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.300
and other hardware to
tools, to major appliances,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.180
garden supplies, doors, windows, toilets,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.590
really any thing you'd need
for a home improvement project.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:25.914
- [Narrator] A typical
Home Depot store stocks

00:01:25.914 --> 00:01:29.640
about 30,000 to 40,000
items throughout the year.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.230
Most locations are around
100, 4,000 square feet.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:36.000
The scale of the store gives
customers the opportunity

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.380
to buy raw materials in bulk
and pick up items quickly.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.470
- They try to be somewhere that you can go

00:01:41.470 --> 00:01:43.100
if you're just an individual

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.680
trying to fix up
something in your kitchen.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.760
They also try to be a
place that you can go

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:51.310
if you're a contractor
trying to buy lumber

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.440
to help renovate somebody's home,

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.730
or if you're a plumber

00:01:54.730 --> 00:01:56.850
that needs all kinds of pipe fittings.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.950
So they really try to be a good source

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.840
on both sides of that equation.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.730
- [Narrator] Home Depot
began when co-founders

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:05.970
Bernie Marcus and Arthur Blank were fired

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:08.570
from a home improvement
company called Handy Dan's.

00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:10.270
They wanted to launch
a store that would be

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:13.470
significantly bigger and
cheaper than competitors.

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:17.210
In 1979, they opened their
first two Home Depot locations

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:18.070
in Atlanta.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.410
- [Man] The Home Depot.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:20.610
- [Narrator] The founders had a vision

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.020
for a home improvement retailer

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.700
that could be a one stop shop for the DIY

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:26.120
or do it yourself customer.

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:28.450
- [Man] You've never
seen anything like it.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.800
- The home improvement
customer to us is unique.

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:31.633
They're a doer.

00:02:31.633 --> 00:02:33.220
That's where that word comes from.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:35.430
- [Narrator] Since it's
founding Home Depot has grown

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.620
into a multi-billion dollar company

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:40.410
that increasingly caters to
the professional contractor,

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:42.430
as well as the DIY consumer.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.140
While many industries like
service and hospitality

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.660
took a hit during the pandemic,

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.240
Home Depot's revenue continued to grow.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:52.390
The pandemic fueled a boom in
the home improvement industry.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.940
As people spent more time and
money on remodeling projects.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.191
- Between middle of 2020
and the middle of 2021

00:02:59.191 --> 00:03:01.010
there were four straight quarters

00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.770
where Home Depot grew its sales

00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:05.002
by more than 20% year over year

00:03:05.002 --> 00:03:08.080
which is a very fast pace for
a large established company.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:09.640
- [Narrator] Home Depot
says they are seeing

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.840
increasing demand for
professional projects

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:12.940
as people feel comfortable

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.460
inviting contractors
back into their homes.

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:18.912
- There's been this buildup of projects

00:03:18.912 --> 00:03:22.120
that require professionals
that more recently

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:23.710
people have been willing to get to.

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:27.160
And that's sort of led to a
second wind of sales growth.

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:32.160
- [Man] What kind of person
would come here at 5:45 a.m.?

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:35.480
Well there's Carly, a carpenter.

00:03:35.480 --> 00:03:37.100
- [Narrator] Home Depot
has positioned itself

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.270
to attract more business
from these contractors

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.320
and home professionals

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:43.170
particularly ones that place big orders.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.920
- [Man] Everything we do, we do for them.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:48.000
- [Narrator] In the 2021 fiscal year,

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:51.030
about 50% of its sales
came from pro customers,

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.850
even though they made up less
than 10% of its customer base.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:59.020
In comparison about 20 to
25% of Lowe's total sales

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.730
come from pro customers
according to the company.

00:04:01.730 --> 00:04:04.390
As a key part of its pro customer strategy

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:07.430
Home Depot has invested $1.2 billion

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:10.390
in expanding its supply chain
and distribution network.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:14.240
The company says it is building
150 new distribution centers

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:16.860
to help speed up the
replenishment of store shelves

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:19.760
and quickly deliver
purchases to customers doors.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.850
Each facility with some as large

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:24.170
as about 14 professional football fields

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.090
can hold a huge amount of inventory

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:29.060
and deliver orders
directly to a project site.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:31.650
- One thing we know that's
important to our pros

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.190
is delivery of product to the job site.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.410
We've shifted our model to a network

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:40.120
of nearly 150 distribution
centers that are engineered

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.350
to deliver for those
big and bulky products

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:44.900
that are unique to the Home
Depot and unique to the pro.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:48.400
Think lumber, think doors,
think windows, think vanities.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.580
We're designing a network
that will deliver those goods

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:56.580
same day or next day to 90% of
the population in our market.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:58.020
- [Narrator] The home improvement giant's

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.150
distribution network works in tandem

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.390
with their online strategy,

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:03.920
giving pro customers more flexible options

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.990
that better align with busy schedules.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.960
- We're one of the largest
e-commerce retailers

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.570
in the country by volume.

00:05:09.570 --> 00:05:11.430
When people come to pick up orders

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:14.100
from our lockers or from our service desk

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.990
they often shop for more
products in the store.

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:20.540
And so that's an economic
flywheel that our website creates

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:21.550
for our company.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.490
- These possibilities have
really helped the company

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.094
grow it sales quite a bit
over the last two years,

00:05:26.094 --> 00:05:30.200
sales from e-commerce channels
have gone up by about 100%.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:31.590
So basically doubled.

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.560
- [Narrator] Though Home
Depot has seen a long period

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.020
of consistent revenue growth,

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:37.950
the home improvement retail
space remains a competitive

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.490
and fragmented market.

00:05:39.490 --> 00:05:42.480
- This is a space where customers

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:44.260
are very sensitive to prices.

00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:47.570
So if one brand is charging a higher price

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.150
for a certain type of equipment

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:51.060
that's something that
buyers could pick up on

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:53.280
and could easily shift
to another retailer.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:56.130
So Home Depot is definitely very sensitive

00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.830
to other big chains to
smaller mom and pop stores.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.460
- [Narrator] The industry
is also sensitive

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:04.700
to economic fluctuations
especially with spending trends

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.070
tied to the housing market.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.270
- Going back to the great recession

00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:10.510
in the financial crisis 10 years ago

00:06:10.510 --> 00:06:11.890
that was a very difficult time

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:13.500
for home improvement retailers,

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.470
a turbulent period for Home Depot.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.330
In the last couple years
to during the pandemic,

00:06:17.330 --> 00:06:21.110
the housing market's been very
strong, certainly a company

00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:24.030
that would be in a very different position

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:25.850
if there was some kind of big downturn

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.623
in the housing market in general.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:31.613
(upbeat music)

